I feint high toward the leading wolf, drawing a defensive snap, then drop low and punch the blade into its throat.

The second wolf lunges from behind, snapping at my right calf. I react instantly, jerking my leg clear and driving an elbow into its snout. As it stumbles off balance, I plunge my dagger through the back of its skull. The final wolf charges; I wait for the jaws to commit, slip sideways under the snap, and bury the steel into its neck.

Space twists like spun glass. The snowy plains fracture and dissolve, snapping our consciousness back into our earthen bodies with the force of a physical impact. We gasp, staggering on the damp gravel of the abandoned mines.

